If you mean the last such index, use binary search:

```c
// Returns the last index i such that arr[i] < target,
// or -1 if none exists. Assumes n >= 0 and arr is sorted.
int find_last_less(const int arr[], int n, int target)
{
    int left = 0, right = n - 1;
    int result = -1;

    while (left <= right) {
        int mid = left + (right - left) / 2;

        if (arr[mid] < target) {
            result = mid;
            left = mid + 1;
        } else {
            right = mid - 1;
        }
    }

    return result;
}
```

This returns a **zero-based index**, handles empty arrays and duplicates, and uses **O(log n)** time and **O(1)** extra space.

