Assistant A closely matches the requested scope and provides a plausible interface requiring normal implementation work. Assistant B is much longer, introduces unsolicited implementation and build instructions, and makes errors throughout all three layers: header, implementation, and usage.

No clarification was essential here: “resize axes” can reasonably mean changing their numeric ranges, while ordinary widget resizing handles the rectangular drawing area. Both answers could have stated that distinction explicitly.

